stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Absent
    Absent --> Pending: complete native record materialized durably
    Pending --> Pending: reason rotates / first log per process only
    Pending --> Pending: other frame context removed / only that hash blocked
    Pending --> Pending: final admission refused / keep queue and retry after 5 seconds
    Pending --> Excluded: exact Owned or existing no-notice policy proof
    Pending --> Expired: same exemption proof + proven closed session
    Pending --> Prepared: direct Unowned + final admission + migration ready
    Prepared --> EffectUnknown: first POST poll / crash before acknowledgement
    EffectUnknown --> Posted: existing history confirmation
    Prepared --> Posted: confirmed POST
    Pending --> Pending: session boundary without exemption proof
    Pending --> Pending: restart replays evidence; one new log allowed
    Excluded --> Excluded: restart preserves terminal proof
    Expired --> Expired: restart preserves terminal proof
    Posted --> Posted: restart preserves posted identity
    note right of Pending
        No timeout erasure. Permanent evidence loss
        is an explicit liveness counterexample.
        Custody/checkpoint and blocked self-wake
        remain WriterWake responsibilities.
    end note
